course: dictionary
lesson: 3066
title: What is an economy?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An economy is the way a country or area makes, buys, sells and uses its money, work and goods. Think of it as one big system: people make things, other people buy them, and money moves between them.
explain: The word has other meanings too. «The family's economy meant turning off lights and reusing paper.» Here economy means careful use of money, so nothing is wasted. The clues in the sentence show which meaning fits.
explain: Sometimes economy describes something cheaper and simpler, like «economy class» on a plane or an «economy pack» of biscuits. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a country, about saving, or about price? That question helps you pick the right meaning.
fact: An economy is the system of how money, work, goods and services are made, bought and sold.
fact: «The economy goes up and down like a slow wave.»
fact: A boom is a time of good times for the economy, when jobs are easy to find.
fact: A recession is when a country's economy shrinks for a while, and jobs become harder to find.
fact: «Negative growth» means the economy is shrinking.
exercise: «The economy goes up and down like a slow wave.» In this sentence, what does economy mean? | *The whole system of making, buying and selling in a country | Bags for keeping coins | Careful use of time
exercise: «We bought the economy pack of pasta because it gave more for the money.» What does economy mean here? | Being very angry about prices | A country's money system | *Cheaper and simpler, a bigger pack that gives better value
exercise: «Dad's careful economy with money kept the family safe in hard times.» What does economy mean here? | A long holiday abroad | Making things in a factory | *Careful use of money so it is not wasted
test: «A recession is when a country's economy shrinks for a while.» What does shrinks mean here? | Moves to another country | Stays exactly the same forever | Gets bigger every day | *Gets smaller
test: On a plane, «economy class» usually means | A seat with the best view of the wings | A seat that costs more than any other | *A cheaper and simpler seat | A seat in the cargo hold
exam: When a country's economy shrinks for a while, what is it called? | Economy class | A boom | *A recession | An economy pack
